# Self-Survey Document Type Matrix — Task Plan & Implementation Log

## Plan
- **High-level goal:** Build the comprehensive, interactive Self-Survey matrix for Program Accreditation with live real-time scoring, section means, parameter means, area means, and official AACCUP rubric.
- **Scope:**
  - Area carousel navigation (Areas I to IX) matching AACCUP institutional/program survey format.
  - Collapsible Rating Scale Reference (NA, 0 to 5) with percentage criteria and standard definitions.
  - Interactive evaluation matrix with DaisyUI `<select>` dropdowns for Item Ratings (IR).
  - Live client-side calculation of System Mean, Implementation Mean, Outcome Mean, Parameter Mean, Total Rating, and Area Mean with `tabular-nums font-mono`.
  - Best Practices textarea per parameter with live reactivity.
  - Prepared By sign-off and Submit action with local storage persistence and submission feedback.
  - Clean Print / Export layout for physical inspection.
- **Key decisions:**
  - Modular component architecture strictly respecting the 150–200 line limit:
    - `SelfSurveyView.vue`: Master orchestrator.
    - `SelfSurveyAreaCarousel.vue`: Horizontal area selection tab strip with completion progress.
    - `RatingScaleReference.vue`: Collapsible AACCUP 1–5 scoring rubric.
    - `SelfSurveyParameterBlock.vue`: Parameter table with S/I/O sections, dropdowns, and sub-means.
    - `SelfSurveySummaryFooter.vue`: Footer bar with Total Rating, Area Mean banner, sign-off input, and submit action.
    - `selfSurveyData.js`: Centralized data definitions for Areas I–IX, parameters, and indicators extracted from institutional survey instruments.
  - Pure Vue 3 reactive computation engine for 0ms lag during scoring.
- **Testing strategy:**
  - Verify calculations: NA exclusion, valid indicator denominators, parameter mean 3-way averaging, and area mean computation.
  - Run `php artisan test` and `npm run build` to ensure zero regressions.

